 "sections_note": "The top-level sections of each policy's own body, in order, as a member reads them (its outline's first level: roman numerals, or capital letters where the order numbers its parts so); the table of contents and a revision memorandum's text are not the body. `heading` is the start of the heading as printed, empty where the text read does not show it (a part number lost or misread by the text layer or the OCR). A Special Order that only replaces passages has the parts it prints; one with no outline has none. Numbered paragraphs (1., 2.) are sections as the outline's other levels are."
}
